// DRAFT page for tpe-* (Transplant Patient in the ED): thrombotic microangiopathy (TMA) in the transplant recipient on a calcineurin inhibitor. Entry node: tpe-tma (summary and citation present). Drug cards for tacrolimus and cyclosporine link to tpe-tma from their Thrombotic microangiopathy row.
// Sources: six FDA labels (DailyMed SPL), ISHLT 2023 heart guideline (heart recipients only; one narrative sentence), AASLD/AST 2024 liver graft-complications guideline (AMR statement, not TMA). NO primary guideline for TMA in transplant recipients exists in the sources read; review papers were not yet available.
// Imports use draft-relative paths; the assembler rewrites them. Module numbers are 0 for the assembler. Detail lives in drafts/tpe-tma-detail.info.ts (InfoPage id tpe-tma-detail).
// Every clinical sentence is SOURCED (cited, grade only where printed) or begins "Editor note:" or "App content:" (a statement about an existing consult, file and line given in the ledger). No immunosuppressant doses.
// "Editor note: call the transplant team ..." appears once in the entry node (body) and once as critical action 3. Ledger: drafts/tpe-tma.ledger.md
import type { DecisionNode } from '../../../src/models/types.js';
import type { CriticalAction } from '../../../src/services/tree-service.js';

